  "licence_text": "\"These databases and this memorandum have been reviewed and cleared for UNLIMITED PUBLIC RELEASE.\" (NSRDEC Memorandum for Record, 14 April 2017). U.S. Government work; no other licence is stated.",
  "url": "https://www.openlab.psu.edu/ansur2/",
  "attribution": "Contains data derived from the 2012 U.S. Army Anthropometric Survey (ANSUR II) public working databases, U.S. Army Natick Soldier Research, Development and Engineering Center.",
  "modification": "Derived/modified: per-subject ratios of each measurement to stature, summarised as the 5th, 50th and 95th percentiles (numpy linear interpolation). Head height is derived as sitting height - eye height sitting + menton-sellion length. No subject rows are included.",
  "caveats": "Military sample: adults only (no children), heavy bodies truncated by fitness standards. Sellion sits a few mm above the pupil, so derived head height is about +-5 mm.",
